{"id":"VHH__LightBox__compounds__LB_directional","collection":"VHH","category":"LightBox/compounds","source_path":"VHH/LightBox/compounds/LB_directional.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::LB_directional"],"counts":{"nodes":48,"connections":92,"values":39,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system. Directionallight - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a directional light. It does this by taking the light direction and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity. Then applying shadow information.","documentation_search":"LB directional Component Compound - this compound is a light in the the LightBox system. Directionallight - This is a diffuse light generator that mimics the lighting from a directional light. It does this by taking the light direction and the mesh surface normal, performing a dot product and multiplying by the light's intensity. Then applying shadow information. The diagnostic tab will hide and show the shadow rays to the light. Input input mesh The object you are lighting. accelerator You need to construct a raycast accelerator from the mesh to plug in here. light direction The direction the light is pointing. If you are using a Maya light, you will need to derive this from it's matrix. directional intensity Intensity and color of the light. icon position The position of the directional icon in world space. directional weight This is an overall multiplier of the output. It is a auto-port, allowing for the input of float , floatArray and scalar field data. Output direction contribution An array of values, per point, of this light's contribution to the lighting. Add this to the point color of your mesh to see the result.","port_names":["accelerator","direction_contribution","directional_intensity","directional_weight","icon_position","icon_scale","input_mesh","light_data","light_direction"],"node_types_search":