_direction***</span>\n<br />The direction the light is pointing.  If you are using a Maya light, you will need to derive this from it's matrix.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***directional_intensity***</span>\n<br />Intensity and color of the light.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***icon_position***</span>\n<br />The position of the directional icon in world space.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***directional_weight***</span>\n<br />This is an overall multiplier of the output.  It is a auto-port, allowing for the input of `float`, `floatArray` and `scalar_field` data.\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***direction_contribution***</span>\n<br />An array of values, per point, of this light's contribution to the lighting.  Add this to the `point_color` of your mesh to see the result.","ports":[{"name":"input_mesh","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"accelerator","direction":"input","type":"Object"},{"name":"light_direction","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"1f","y":"-1f","z":"1f"}},{"name":"directional_intensity","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0.400000006f","z":"1f"}},{"name":"icon_position","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"icon_scale","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"directional_weight","direction":"input","type":null,"default":"1f"},{"name":"light_data","direction":"output","type":null},{"name":"direction_contribution","direction":"output","type":null}],"terminal_states":[{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::final","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::proxy","enabled":"true"},{"name":"Core::Graph::terminal::diagnostic","enabled":"false"}],"counts":{"nodes":48,"connections":92,"values":39,"nested_compounds":8},"node_types":{"Unknown":7,"Core::Math::multiply":3,"Core::Graph::pass":3,"Core::Logic::if":2,"Geometry::Common::interpret_auto_port_as_scalar":2,"C